  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancement of the Horn of Africa Groundwater Data Hub</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Horn of Africa (HoA) is a fragile region, facing intricate development issues such as fragility, conflict, and violence (FCV), alongside food crises and challenging socio-political and economic conditions. Famine pockets perpetuate food insecurity across the region. Climate-induced shocks are escalating tensions over scarce natural resources, particularly regarding water and land. Groundwater holds a crucial role in fortifying climate resilience. Unfortunately, this resource remains largely underutilised. The Horn of Africa Groundwater for Resilience Program (GW4R) addresses these challenges at the regional level, with the objective of strengthening sustainable groundwater service delivery through applied research and expert technical support for the GW4R Program.</narrative>
  </description>
